 :doc/body "# OpenRouter provider application — Murakumo\n\nStatus: DRAFT / NOT SUBMITTED. This replaces the September 1 application narrative, not the independent Basho/Hokusai product roadmap. Do not send until the gates below are evidenced.\n\n## Backend revision requested 2026-09-08\nCORRECTION: the owner specifies Murakumo fleet as primary; Modal is a stability backup, with failback to fleet after recovery. The preceding interpretation that Modal replaces fleet was incorrect. Existing b70 evidence remains applicable to that fixed fleet candidate. Modal evidence qualifies only its backup leg, and Modal account access is not a prerequisite for continued fleet testing. See business-openrouter-fleet-primary-modal-backup-20260908. The Modal cost, retention and contract research remains supporting backup analysis; it does not redefine the primary offering.\n\n## Proposed offering\nProduct concept: Slow, but cheap. Murakumo is a cost-first distributed compute cluster for workloads that can tolerate waiting: document processing, offline generation and other deadline-tolerant jobs. This is a product direction, not evidence that the currently qualified single b70 backend performs multi-node model-parallel inference.\nThe candidate price is USD 0.10 per million input tokens and USD 0.40 per million output tokens. These are proposed catalog prices, not proof of profitability or a lowest-market-price claim. Historical unit-cost estimates for another model cannot validate this dense 27B candidate.\nMurakumo proposes a self-hosted upstream text model, qwen3.8-27b-throughput-b70, served through https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/chat/completions. It is not an original model or a proprietary fine-tune. The advertised alias murakumo-main is unsuitable for this application because its response can identify a different backend. Basho's current upstream relay and the untrained Hokusai artifact are not part of this proposal.\n\nCandidate catalog: https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/openrouter/models. This separate projection uses the official ModelDocumentV2 schema version 2.4 and deliberately reports is_ready=false. It makes no ZDR, certified-compliance, dedicated-capacity or proprietary-training claim. The existing /v1/models remains the product discovery surface, not the application catalog.\n\n## Evidence as of 2026-09-08\nTwo initial public requests to the fixed candidate returned HTTP 200, the requested model ID, correct changing marker text, stop, and consistent positive prompt/completion usage. The streaming request also supplied [DONE]. These are low-volume protocol checks, not a model-weight attestation, uptime history or a load test.\nThe candidate catalog is checked against a vendored official schema, including negative cases. The smoke host rejects wrong models, missing usage, incomplete streams and oversized responses. It writes timestamps, model identity, timing, token counts and pass/fail, not customer prompts or generated content.\n\n## Qualification plan\nOpenRouter synchronous traffic uses available capacity with early HTTP 429 and Retry-After when saturated, rather than an unbounded queue. Slow processing keeps SSE connections alive; keepalive comments are not generated tokens and must not count toward TTFT. Long queued work belongs to an explicitly asynchronous product contract with a deadline, cancellation and a price limit.\nRun scripts/api-smoke.cljs --provider-sample every 15 minutes, making one non-streaming and one streaming request sequentially, with a 45-second timeout. Append results to ~/.murakumo/openrouter-b70-samples.jsonl. Report with --provider-report.\nOur internal low-volume observation gate is seven days, at least 1,000 non-429 requests (at least 500 in each mode), at least 99.5% correctness success excluding HTTP 429, no observation gap over 45 minutes, latency percentiles retained as observations rather than pass/fail limits. Policy slow-cheap-v2 supersedes the previous internal 10-second completion / 5-second TTFT gate at the owner's direction; historical samples remain unchanged. The 45-second tiny-probe deadline still rejects unfinished probes and is not a universal product SLA. HTTP 429 is reported separately, never erased. These are internal targets, not OpenRouter's published acceptance criteria. A rolling window permits recovery from old failures; sleep or a stopped scheduler creates a coverage gap.\nEven when this observation gate passes, production-ready remains false. A small repeated prompt cannot establish long-context quality, parallel-load capacity, billing correctness or outage recovery.\n\n## Remaining submission gates\n1. Artifact identity and published license declarations VERIFIED on 2026-09-08: live SHA-256 matches the pinned lmstudio-community GGUF; Q4_K_M and Apache-2.0 source/card declarations checked. Conversion reproduction and exact quantizer source-commit attestation remain unverified. The public 16,384-token budget and one-token-over-limit rejection passed. See business-openrouter-b70-qualification-evidence-20260908.\n2. One long-context boundary request and one two-request concurrent pair passed on 2026-09-08. One bounded public saturation experiment now returns early 429 with Retry-After: 5 in 45 ms, with both admitted streams completing and a fresh request succeeding afterwards; see business-openrouter-b70-overload-resolution-20260908 and API PR #239. A separate approximately five-minute sequential run completed 40/40 requests. API #241 fixes delayed prefill abort; live midstream cancellation reached the origin and released its slot within 4.168 seconds, confirmed by cancel-task logs. Sustained parallel load, repeated cold-prefill cancellation, atomic admission races, backend restart and matching-model Modal failover/failback remain open. See business-openrouter-provider-blockers-20260908. Reserve capacity so existing workloads cannot consume the promised offer. Establish supported request parameters with measured results.\n3. Establish the OpenRouter credential, authorization and per-provider accounting boundary. Current anonymous public smoke success does not prove authenticated partner isolation or billable metering.\n4. Publish approved, final privacy/retention and terms pages covering edge, inference origin, asynchronous storage and operational logs. Current public legal pages are marked DRAFT; no whole-service ZDR claim is justified. Public URLs: https://murakumo.cloud/legal-privacy and https://murakumo.cloud/legal-terms.\n5. Contracting entity confirmed by the owner as AWAI Network LLC (see identity section below). Confirm billing contact and either automatic top-up or invoicing with reconciliation. OpenRouter provider documentation allows either payment mechanism; monthly invoicing is not the only documented path. Do not infer legal or invoice readiness from a company name on a website.\n6. Finish seven-day observation and attach the raw ledger hash, UTC interval, request counts, 429 count, failure causes, throughput and latency percentiles. Cross-check public catalog against actual deployment.\n7. Verify candidate-specific cost per successful useful output, including retries, idle capacity, electricity, hardware amortization, operator payments and edge/storage fees. Do not reuse the older sparse-model cost estimate as proof for the dense 27B candidate.\n8. Rewrite the final submission from verified evidence, then submit and retain an external receipt. A draft, merged PR, deployed endpoint or scheduler is not an application receipt.\n\n## Sources\nhttps://openrouter.ai/providers/apply\nhttps://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/community/for-providers\nhttps://openrouter.ai/docs/assets/provider-monitor-schema-v2.openapi.json\nPrevious original-model plan: adr-2609011842-awai-japanese-models-openrouter-provider-application.\n\n\n## Contracting identity confirmed by owner — 2026-09-08\nLegal entity: AWAI Network, L.L.C. (formation certificate spelling). Business-account name: AWAI Network LLC.\nPublic business name: AWAI Network, L.L.C.\nBusiness website: https://awai.network/ .\nPreviously supplied business/support address: 131 Continental Dr, Suite 305, Newark, DE 19713, United States. The later company-contact section distinguishes the Tokyo company address from this registered-office/support address.\nSource: owner-provided business-account information in this conversation. This confirms which entity the owner intends to contract through; it is not an independent registry lookup or proof of the signer's authority.\nThe owner states that EIN and other business information have been supplied to the account provider, but at that earlier stage no EIN value, state registration number, billing-contact email or support telephone was included. The document evidence below supersedes the missing formation and EIN-assignment evidence. Do not invent or publish these values. Do not reuse a historical registration number without verification. Obtain any sensitive identifier only if the actual onboarding process requires it, through its private channel.\nThe Modal invoice's junkawasakicom workspace label is not a different contracting entity declaration. Confirm the applicable Modal account agreement/Service Order against AWAI Network LLC. OpenRouter payment mechanism and billing contact remain open.\n\n\n## Document evidence supplied by owner — 2026-09-08\nReviewed all pages of the original PDFs using extraction and rendered-page inspection. The certificate states AWAI Network, L.L.C. as the formed legal name; use this exact spelling for legal contracting fields. AWAI Network LLC is the business-account and IRS spelling supplied by the owner.\nDelaware file number: 10704996. Formation filed July 20, 2026 at 4:24 p.m.; certified copy dated July 21, 2026. Registered office: 131 Continental Dr, Suite 305, Newark, DE 19713, New Castle County, United States. Registered agent: Legalinc Corporate Services Inc. The formation page is signed Kawasaki Jun, Authorized Person. The owner separately designated this same address for business/support; the certificate itself describes a registered office, not a compute location.\nFormation source: /Users/junkawasaki/Downloads/AWAINetworkLLC - Approved Certificate of Formation.pdf (2 pages). SHA-256 bc9ceea6020138d27ebd5c1e1e9cbac0d1fbd3ba42185ee9a7f077a034f5db70.\nThe two files named AWAINetworkLLC - 147c Letter_Approved SS-4 (1).pdf and AWAINetworkLLC - 147c Letter_Approved SS-4 (3).pdf are byte-identical, each one page, SHA-256 4aef4648ba62ae421923603a0a794b843e92dd5cc4fceb91e3323ce112923c9f. They are an IRS EIN Unit fax dated August 5, 2026, naming AWAI Network LLC and recording an EIN assignment on that date. The EIN value was visually read but is deliberately not reproduced in this repository or public application narrative; consult the owner-supplied original privately when onboarding requires it.\nDespite their filenames, the visible document is not an approved SS-4 or a 147C letter. It expressly states that it is not the official EIN verification document and that a CP575 notice will follow. Record EIN assignment evidence as received, but do not mark official EIN verification documentation as received. If a counterparty requires that document, use an actual CP575 or 147C; do not assume every application requires one.\nThis resolves the earlier lack of source documents for formation/name/file number/registered office, and lack of an EIN assignment source. Document inspection is not an online Delaware authenticity/current-status check, independent IRS validation, proof of ownership or general contracting/signing authority. Billing contact, chosen payment rail and applicable Modal agreement remain separate open items. No documents or identifiers were transmitted externally; the application remains unsubmitted.\n\n\n## Company contact supplied by owner — 2026-09-08\nCompany-account name: AWAI Network LLC. Legal name on formation certificate: AWAI Network, L.L.C. Entity type: Delaware LLC. Formation date July 20, 2026; Delaware file number 10704996. The owner-supplied EIN matches the previously inspected IRS assignment fax; its value remains excluded from repository text and public application narrative.\nCompany representative: Kawasaki Jun (owner-confirmed role). Company telephone: +81 80 4280 1991, normalized +818042801991. Do not infer a separate billing contact or signing mandate solely from this field.\nCompany address, transcribed as supplied: postal code 150-0001; Tokyo; Shibuya; 2-2-39; Japan. Do not invent an omitted town/street or building name, or replace this company address with the registered office.\nDelaware registered office remains 131 Continental Dr, Suite 305, Newark, DE 19713, United States, as supported by the formation certificate. The owner previously designated this same Newark address for customer support; retain it as the support address until changed. Keep company address, registered office, support address and compute/data-processing location as distinct fields.\nThis resolves the previously missing company representative, company telephone and company-address information through owner confirmation. It is not independent phone/address verification and does not turn the IRS assignment fax into CP575/147C. Billing email/contact designation, OpenRouter payment mechanism and applicable Modal agreement remain open. No account settings or public legal pages were changed, and no application was submitted.\n"}]
